---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="About this blog"
	pubDate={new Date('2025-05-30')}
>
	<p>
		This blog tracks the latest developments in <strong>AI Agent Architecture</strong> —
		multi-agent orchestration, tool use, function calling, planning, memory, and everything
		that makes LLM-based agents work in production.
	</p>

	<p>
		Every day, we scan 50+ tweets from X's "For You" feed, arXiv papers, Zhihu articles,
		and Semantic Scholar to surface the most important updates. Content is filtered through
		a 4-tier system: company updates, industry leaders, trending posts, and rising stars.
	</p>

	<p>
		Posts are published bilingually in Chinese and English.
	</p>

	<h2>Topics We Cover</h2>

	<ul>
		<li>Multi-agent orchestration and reliability</li>
		<li>Coding agents (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, etc.)</li>
		<li>Agent frameworks (LangChain, CrewAI, AutoGen, etc.)</li>
		<li>Tool use and function calling patterns</li>
		<li>Agent memory and context management</li>
		<li>Planning and reasoning architectures</li>
		<li>MCP (Model Context Protocol) ecosystem</li>
		<li>Agent evaluation and benchmarking</li>
		<li>Production deployment and engineering practices</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Built With</h2>

	<p>
		Powered by <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a>, deployed on
		<a href="https://pages.github.com">GitHub Pages</a>. Content collected and curated
		automatically every day at 9:00 AM CST.
	</p>
</Layout>
